# Clean standalone charm decay table derived from decays_charm.data.
# Canonical metadata: decays_charm_bottom.dat (PDG 2026) and the tracked light table.
# Legacy compact names are retained; IDs and physical metadata are canonical where available.
# Format: id name mass width degeneracy B S C Bot I Q n_channels
# Channel: id n_daughters BR d1 d2 d3 d4 d5
# Commented source channels are excluded. Branching fractions are absolute and not renormalized.
# Excluded unsupported parents: Dc2750 quartet, Ds2700 pair, Ds2860 pair (30 channels).
# Removed eight Ds2573 -> D(*) pi pi channels that violate strangeness.
# Corrected K0 to anti-K0 on source lines 4-7 and 125, and D0 to anti-D0 on line 116.
# Four Lc2595 -> Sc2455 pi modes are below pole threshold but reopen within 4 widths.
# A self-channel denotes a model terminal, not a physically stable particle.
# The cascade skips zero-mass photon daughter spectra; massive partners still propagate.
# Contents: 91 particle headers, 102 physical decay rows, and 21 terminal self rows.
# Private IDs >= 10090001 are collision-checked model IDs; their zero widths are legacy placeholders.
# The source supplies no conjugate partners for private Om states or Xic2970.
# Private families: Lc2765=+/-10090001 Lc2860=+/-10090002 Lc2940=+/-10090003
# Sc2800 charge families: +/-10090101, +/-10090102, +/-10090103
